  improved performance (p < .001) on aspects of the GoNoGo task (p < .02) and on three CANTAB tasks which together      
  contributed to a "recognition memory" component identified through principal components analysis (delayed matching    
  to sample [DMtS], pattern and spatial recognition). There were no effects on other, high or low "executive demand"    
  tasks (p > .05). GoNoGo performance improvements were the only neuropsychopharmacological changes associated with     
