│ Review title: Methylphenidate for children and adolescents with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD)      │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review background:                                                                                                   │
│ Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) is one of the most commonly diagnosed and treated psychiatric        │
│ disorders in childhood. Typically, children and adolescents with ADHD find it difficult to pay attention and they    │
│ are hyperactive and impulsive. Methylphenidate is the psychostimulant most often prescribed, but the evidence on     │
│ benefits and harms is uncertain. This is an update of our comprehensive systematic review on benefits and harms      │
│ published in 2015.                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review objective:                                                                                                    │
│ To assess the beneficial and harmful effects of methylphenidate for children and adolescents with ADHD.              │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Selection criteria:                                                                                                  │
